**R1. Actor-driven selection and allocation: ADDRESSED.** The market hand reaches, grips and releases the actual chosen product (`HouseholdMarketChoice/MarketShopper.tsx:12`, `getShopperPose.ts:20`, `getShopperPose.ts:37`). The recipient hand follows the selected unit, withdraws continuously and counts completed pulls on the receipt (`RecipientConfirmedHandover/getRecipientPose.ts:21`, `getRecipientPose.ts:37`, `HandoverReceiptRow.tsx:14`). Donor supports visibly tip, and the coordinator grips a scoop carrying the exact attributed batch (`PooledDonorAllocation/DonorTray.tsx:18`, `getAllocationTokens.ts:17`, `AllocationCoordinator.tsx:28`). Added assertions inspect emitted hands, arms, supports and object positions rather than ownership annotations alone. N1 below is new handling breakage, separate from the original absence of actor actions.

**R2. Loaded-carrier travel: ADDRESSED.** Per-carrier positions now wait, advance and stop independently (`AidCargoModeHandoff/getCarrierPosition.ts:10`). Parcel positions derive from the active source and receiving carrier (`getCargoPosition.ts:17`). Three-carrier middle travel occupies frames 66-80, followed by the second handoff and final travel at 112-132. Two-carrier final travel occupies 66-96. The new test checks emitted carrier movement, every parcel's fixed load offset and the parked first carrier across all fixtures (`AidCargoModeHandoff.test.ts:137`).

All source references are relative to `apps/ava-video-producer/src/stock/presets/`. Review target: fix base `5a35b03b563274836e4944d747eff0f31ec216e8`, head `375c3d38725002f0ab835d251f38e66d15dc85da`.

## New breakage in the fix diff

**Important N1. Keep the scoop on canvas when a small request precedes a larger batch.** `PooledDonorAllocation/getAllocationHandling.ts:20` sizes the scoop from the next request's token bounds, while `getAllocationHandling.ts:26` and `getAllocationHandling.ts:31` anchor that width at the previous request's hand before pickup. A schema-valid two-request allocation of 1 then 13 credits produces an opaque scoop from x=-179 to x=83 at frame 82. `AllocationCoordinator.tsx:44` emits that path, clipping 179 pixels beyond the left canvas edge. The new all-frame clearance check only traverses existing fixture distributions (`registerFundingActionAssertions.ts:19`), so it misses this accepted concentration/order combination. Reposition the empty support within the canvas before pickup, preserving continuous hand contact during loaded travel. Add this uneven request order to the focused geometry regression.

